{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\n\nconst ll INF = 9'000'000'000'000'000'000LL;\n\nll fib_like[17], target, best;\n\nll abs_val(ll x) { return x < 0 ? -x : x; }\n\nvoid dfs(int idx, ll cur_sum, ll cost) {\n    if (cur_sum == 0) {\n        best = min(best, cost);\n        return;\n    }\n    if (idx == 0) return;\n\n    for (int d = -10; d <= 10; ++d) {\n        ll new_sum = cur_sum + d * fib_like[idx];\n        if (new_sum > 0) {\n            dfs(idx - 1, new_sum, cost + abs_val(d) * idx);\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (int d = -10; d <= 10; ++d) {\n        ll new_sum = cur_sum + d * fib_like[idx];\n        if (new_sum == 0) {\n            dfs(idx - 1, new_sum, cost + abs_val(d) * idx);\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (int d = 10; d >= -10; --d) {\n        ll new_sum = cur_sum + d * fib_like[idx];\n        if (new_sum < 0) {\n            dfs(idx - 1, new_sum, cost + abs_val(d) * idx);\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    cin >> target;\n\n    fib_like[1] = 1;\n    for (int i = 2; i <= 16; ++i)\n        fib_like[i] = fib_like[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n\n    best = INF;\n    dfs(16, target, 0);\n\n    cout << best << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10000)\n\nINF = 9_000_000_000_000_000_000\n\nfib_like = [0] * 17\ntarget = 0\nbest = INF\n\ndef abs_val(x):\n    return -x if x < 0 else x\n\ndef dfs(idx, cur_sum, cost):\n    global best\n    if cur_sum == 0:\n        if cost < best:\n            best = cost\n        return\n    if idx == 0:\n        return\n\n    # First loop: d from -10 to 10, looking for new_sum > 0\n    for d in range(-10, 11):\n        new_sum = cur_sum + d * fib_like[idx]\n        if new_sum > 0:\n            dfs(idx - 1, new_sum, cost + abs_val(d) * idx)\n            break\n\n    # Second loop: d from -10 to 10, looking for new_sum == 0\n    for d in range(-10, 11):\n        new_sum = cur_sum + d * fib_like[idx]\n        if new_sum == 0:\n            dfs(idx - 1, new_sum, cost + abs_val(d) * idx)\n            break\n\n    # Third loop: d from 10 down to -10, looking for new_sum < 0\n    for d in range(10, -11, -1):\n        new_sum = cur_sum + d * fib_like[idx]\n        if new_sum < 0:\n            dfs(idx - 1, new_sum, cost + abs_val(d) * idx)\n            break\n\ndef main():\n    global target, best\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    target = int(data[0])\n\n    fib_like[1] = 1\n    for i in range(2, 17):\n        fib_like[i] = fib_like[i-1] * 10 + 1\n\n    best = INF\n    dfs(16, target, 0)\n\n    print(best)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00010740180005086586, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0699617937207222, -9.643566590966657e-05, -0.6326161026954651, -0.25